          "code": "PRJ_PJO_LLM_EXCEPTION_HANDLER",
          "id": "1781073913695",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781073913699_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an enterprise workflow assistant.\n\nAnalyze this error payload:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJO_BO_FUNCTION_CALL_BUDGET_BOSS_AI.$error.$info}} or {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJO_LLM_RESPONSE_GENERATOR_BUDGET.$error.$info}}\n\nGenerate a JSON response that follows the Chat Widget proposed schema.\n\nThe response must use:\n- Top-level agent response schema\n- display_type = \"text\"\n- display_sequence = 1\n- A short, non-technical, human-understandable message in the text field\n\nThe message is for business users, not developers.\n\n### MESSAGE STYLE RULES\n\nWrite the message in simple business language.\n\nDo not expose technical details such as:\n- HTTP status codes\n- Exception names\n- Stack traces\n- Token counts\n- Model limits\n- Prompt sizes\n- API names\n- Internal node names\n- Component names\n- Workflow implementation details\n- Raw error text\n- Error codes such as start_generation_failed, Bad Request, 400, timeout exception, null pointer, etc.\n\nConvert technical failures into general user-friendly wording.\n\nExamples:\n- Instead of: \"The prompt exceeds the model maximum token length and returned 400 Bad Request.\"\n  Say: \"A technical issue occurred while processing the request. Please try narrowing the request or reducing the amount of information included.\"\n\n- Instead of: \"CALL_BUDGET_BOSS_AI failed with timeout exception.\"\n  Say: \"A technical issue occurred while retrieving the budget information. Please try again.\"\n\n- Instead of: \"RESPONSE_GENERATOR_BUDGET failed because input data was null.\"\n  Say: \"The request could not be completed because required budget information was missing.\"\n\n### ANALYSIS RULES\n\n- Summarize only what a business user needs to know.\n- Keep the message accurate but non-technical.\n- If the error indicates missing or empty data, say that required information was missing.\n- If the error indicates timeout, service failure, model failure, API failure, or system exception, say that a technical issue occurred.\n- If the error indicates too much input, prompt length, context length, or token limit, say that the request included too much information to process.\n- If the error indicates invalid input, malformed request, or bad request, say that the request could not be processed in its current form.\n- If the root cause cannot be determined, say that the request could not be completed due to a technical issue.\n- Do not speculate beyond the provided error information.\n- Keep the text field to 1â2 short sentences.\n- Do not tell the user to contact engineering, support, logs, APIs, or developers.\n- Do not include troubleshooting details unless they are business-user friendly.\n\n### OUTPUT RULES\n\n- Return valid JSON only.\n- Do not return plain text.\n- Do not return markdown.\n- Do not wrap the JSON in a code block.\n- Do not include trailing commas.\n- Escape quotes and line breaks correctly inside JSON strings.\n- The text field must contain only the user-friendly message.\n- The text field must not contain raw technical error details.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON structure:\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"enterprise_error_analysis_assistant\",\n  \"intent\": \"error_summary\",\n  \"schema_version\": \"1\",\n  \"title\": \"Unable to Complete Request\",\n  \"description\": \"User-friendly summary of the workflow issue\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"<ISO-8601 timestamp>\",\n  \"agent_response\": [\n    {\n      \"display_type\": \"text\",\n      \"display_sequence\": 1,\n      \"heading\": \"Unable to Complete Request\",\n      \"text\": \"<1-2 sentence non-technical user-friendly message>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n### FIELD RULES\n\n- timestamp must be the current timestamp in ISO-8601 format if available from the runtime; otherwise use an empty string.\n- If the error payload is null, empty, or does not contain enough information, set text to: \"The request could not be completed due to a technical issue. Please try again.\"\n- If the error indicates too much input, set text to: \"The request included too much information to process. Please try narrowing the request and try again.\"\n- If the error indicates missing information, set text to: \"The request could not be completed because required budget information was missing. Please review the request and try again.\"\n- If the error indicates a timeout or temporary service failure, set text to: \"A technical issue occurred while retrieving the budget information. Please try again.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
